<title>BELGIUM: FULL TEXT - PIXTECH EARNINGS.</title>
<headline>FULL TEXT - PIXTECH EARNINGS.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-02-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Here is a summary of PixTech's</p>
<p>statement on fourth quarter and fiscal year 1996 results:</p>
<p>Revenues for the fourth quarter of fiscal 1996 were $1.0</p>
<p>million, compared with $5.9 million in the fourth quarter of</p>
<p>1995. Revenues for fiscal year 1996 were $7.6 million, compared</p>
<p>with $11.5 million in fiscal 1995. Net loss for the fourth</p>
<p>quarter of 1996 was $4.3 million or a loss of ($0.53) per share.</p>
<p>Net loss for fiscal year 1996 was $11.7 million or a loss of</p>
<p>($1.44) per share.</p>
<p>			 Three months ended	   Year ended</p>
<p>		     Dec 31  Sep 30   Dec 31  Dec 31  Dec 31</p>
<p>			1996     1996    1995    1996    1995</p>
<p>Revenues:</p>
<p>-Cooperation and</p>
<p>license revenues  $207    $707   $5,006   $5,440  $9,865</p>
<p>-product sales     363	67	662	791     808</p>
<p>-other revenues    421	11	195    1,413     840</p>
<p>Total Revenues     991     785    5,863    7,644  11,513</p>
<p>Cost of revenues</p>
<p>-Licences fees</p>
<p> and  royalties    (45)     --     (714)     (45) (1,314)</p>
<p>Gross Margin	 946     785    5,149    7,599  10,199</p>
<p>Total operating</p>
<p>expenses	   5,288   5,208    5,334   19,639  19,477</p>
<p>Loss from</p>
<p>operations	(4,342) (4,423)    (185) (12,040) (9,278)</p>
<p>Income tax benefit ---     ---    1,605	---   2,720</p>
<p>Net income(Loss)(4,316) (4,557)   1,579  (11,718) (6,305)</p>
<p>     per share   $(.53)  $(.56)    $.20   $(1.44)  $(.82)</p>
<p>Shares used in computing</p>
<p>net income (mln) 8,141   8,141    8,161    8,138   7,697</p>
<p>Separately today, PixTech announced the closing of a $24</p>
<p>million round of financing. The company raised $17 million</p>
<p>through a public offering in Europe, $5 million through a</p>
<p>private placement with United Microelectronics Corporation (the</p>
<p>parent company of Unipac) and $2 million through a private</p>
<p>placement with Motorola Inc.</p>
<p>&quot;The milestones we have recently achieved put PixTech on the</p>
<p>right track toward production of a large volume of</p>
<p>field-emission displays,&quot; said Jean-Luc Grand-Clement,</p>
<p>president, chairman and chief executive officer.</p>
<p>-- Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6810, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
